NO THIRD-PARTY IMAGES ARE REDISTRIBUTED HERE
--------------------------------------------
This repository distributes no image files. What it distributes is the case
manifests, the ground-truth labels, the attribution records, and the evaluation
tooling. Every case names its image by SHA-256; the bytes are put on disk by
whoever runs the benchmark. Continuous integration fails the build if any image
binary is committed anywhere in the repository, with no exception for the suite
directories, because a link-only image lands in the same place as a bundled one
and no licence grants us the right to redistribute it.


BUNDLED CASES
-------------
A case marked "bundled" references an image published under a redistributable
licence: CC0, CC-BY, MIT, or Apache-2.0. The original source and licence of
every such image are recorded per case in its suite's provenance file --
ATTRIBUTION.csv for openfield_v1, SOURCES.csv for clean_v1 -- under
tracks/diagnosis/suites/. The operator supplies the bytes from a local copy of
the upstream dataset and materialises them with `agribench stage`, which
matches files by content digest.

Those images are not covered by this repository's Apache-2.0 licence. They
remain under the licence their publisher declared, and any copy or
redistribution of them must preserve the attribution recorded there.
Licences are as declared upstream; we relied on the
publisher's declaration and did not independently verify that each publisher
held the rights it claimed.


LINK-ONLY CASES
---------------
A case marked "link-only" carries a URL and nothing else: no image bytes, and no
licence to any. It is a reference. The operator downloads the file from the
origin, directly, under whatever terms that origin sets. This repository grants
no rights to that content, makes no representation about it, and never contains
it. The recorded SHA-256 digest exists only so that a link which starts serving
different bytes is rejected rather than silently scored.


